KG42.register("source_edge_archive-7c14127a176d0ee5a2ae35d7",{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R003::E::v141-c-R003-E001","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","rule_ref":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R003","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E001","source":"bidding.demand","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"KG31-e3df7b859b17cba0","target":"KG31-623d45f464e9bce4","source_occurrence_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R003::V::bidding.demand","target_occurrence_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","source_unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M01::bidding.demand","target_unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Coordinator infrastructure obligations in the described local P2P framework. | Coordinator intervention under the paper's heuristic convergence techniques. | Limits of the coordinator's modeled remit in the studied P2P framework. | SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g06-e12","v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"26323983c5bd39399cfbb07eaf95dc757b4b1d98d483ce8da883b4fcadd8b17e","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"The coordinator must reject requested-energy bids exceeding the prescribed ramping rate, thereby limiting demand-bid updates. Scope: Proposed practical enforcement of ramping-rate step length control in P2P energy bidding. Condition: The proposed enforcement rule is adopted and a bid exceeds the prescribed ramping rate. The coordinator limits demand-bid updates by uniformly randomly selecting participants whose energy bids must remain unchanged for that iteration. Scope: Iterative energy bidding using the bid-count form of step length control. Condition: Bid-count control is adopted; the restriction applies to participants selected for the forbidden-update set at the current iteration. Internal prices motivate updates to Prosumer A's submitted demand schedule to use excess local PV generation from Prosumer B. Scope: Appendix B's illustrated SDR interaction: Prosumer A's heater-demand schedule submitted to the coordinator. Condition: The unequal hourly internal buying prices in the illustrated iterations. Participants must submit their requested-energy quantities as part of the energy bids required at every iteration. Scope: Requested-energy quantities within SDR energy bids. The current requested-energy bid must lie within the previous bid plus or minus the ramping rate times the previous bid's absolute value. The resulting interval is clipped to the bid's lower and upper limits. Scope: Requested-energy bid updates in the iterative simulation's ramping-rate step length control. Condition: The ramping-rate form of step length control is adopted. Only rmp′ × 100% of energy bids may change, and each permitted demand-bid change is also restricted to ± rmp′ × 100%. Scope: Illustrated combined bid-count and ramping-rate step length control. Condition: The combined control with the broader ramping rate rmp′ is adopted. Demand bidding is assumed to be conducted on a day-ahead basis. Scope: SDR bidding in the paper's two GB residential case-study sets, with accurate generation and demand forecasts assumed. Demand-bidding iteration must terminate at the iteration limit, including when bids have not converged. Scope: Demand-bidding iteration under the paper's proposed last-defence mechanism. Condition: The predefined maximum iteration count is reached, whether or not convergence has been achieved.","target_definition":"Requested quantities represented in the SDR energy-bid profile are submitted to the local coordinator at every iteration. Scope: SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region. Condition: The submitted profile contains a nonnegative net-energy bid at the relevant time step. Offered quantities represented in the SDR energy-bid profile are submitted to the local coordinator at every iteration. Scope: SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region. Condition: The submitted profile contains a negative net-energy bid at the relevant time step. The coordinator must provide and operate the trading platform and its associated metering mechanisms. Scope: Coordinator infrastructure obligations in the described local P2P framework. The coordinator does not control devices directly and applies unified rules fairly to all participants. Scope: Coordinator intervention under the paper's heuristic convergence techniques. Condition: When the heuristic techniques interfere with participants' control of their devices. Handling physical-network problems such as overvoltage and congestion is outside the coordinator's modeled remit and is deferred to further research. Scope: Limits of the coordinator's modeled remit in the studied P2P framework.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Requested quantities represented in the SDR energy-bid profile are submitted to the local coordinator at every iteration. Scope: SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region. Condition: The submitted profile contains a nonnegative net-energy bid at the relevant time step.","expression":"e^{bid} = \\left\\{ e_t^{bid} \\mid e_t^{bid} = \\left( \\sum_{\\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f} x_{\\delta,t}^{*} \\right) + \\left( \\frac{x_t^{ch*}}{\\eta^{ch}} + x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis} \\right) + P_t^{must\\text{-}run} - P_{PV,t},\\; t \\in T \\right\\} \\quad (A18); \\quad \\mathcal{PA}^{+}_{t} = \\{ n \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \\ge 0,\\; n \\in \\mathcal{PA} \\} \\quad (A23)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-04","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p26-c2r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":26,"printed_page":"1018","section":"A.2.1","anchor_text":"p g y ⎫ ∈ T ⎬⎭ (A18) he decision-making model consisting of Formulas (A1)–(A17). With the energy ell","equation_id":"A18","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-26.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In the SDR mechanism, prosumers are required to provide energy bids for the coordinator at every iteration. Specifically, based on the results of the decision-making model presented in Section A.1, the energy bid of a prosumer is given by\n\ne^{bid} = \\left\\{ e_t^{bid} \\mid e_t^{bid} = \\left( \\sum_{\\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f} x_{\\delta,t}^* \\right) + \\left( \\frac{x_t^{ch*}}{\\eta^{ch}} + x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis} \\right) + P_t^{must-run} - P_{PV,t}, t \\in T \\right\\}  (A18)\n\nin which x^* = \\{x_{\\delta,t}^*, x_t^{ch*}, x_t^{dis*}\\}, \\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f, t \\in T are the optimal solution of the decision-making model consisting of Formulas (A1)-(A17)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-05","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p26-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":26,"printed_page":"1018","section":"A.2.1","anchor_text":"(A22) (A23) il price between the coordinator and the retailer as illustrated in Fig. 2; SDR haring r","equation_id":"A19-A23","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-26.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"With the energy bids from all the prosumers, the coordinator calculates the internal selling price by\n\np_t^{sell} = \\begin{cases} \\frac{r_t^{export} \\cdot r_t^{retail}}{(r_t^{retail} - r_t^{export}) \\cdot SDR_t + r_t^{export}}, & 0 \\le SDR_t \\le 1 \\\\ r_t^{export}, & SDR_t > 1 \\end{cases}  (A19)\n\nand the internal buying price by\n\np_t^{buy} = \\begin{cases} p_t^{sell} \\cdot SDR_t + r_t^{retail}(1 - SDR_t), & 0 \\le SDR_t \\le 1 \\\\ r_t^{export}, & SDR_t > 1 \\end{cases}  (A20)\n\nin which\n\nSDR_t = \\frac{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^-} |e_{n,t}^{bid}|}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^+} e_{n,t}^{bid}}  (A21)\n\nwhere\n\n\\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^- = \\{ n \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \u003c 0, n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A} \\}  (A22)\n\nand\n\n\\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^+ = \\{ n \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \\ge 0, n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A} \\}.  (A23)\n\nIn Formulas (A19)-(A23), r_t^{export} and r_t^{retail} are the export and retail price between the coordinator and the retailer as illustrated in Fig. 2; SDR represents the supply and demand ratio of the whole P2P energy sharing region. Formulas (A19)-(A23) establish the pricing model in the coordinator agent under the SDR mechanism."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Coordinator infrastructure obligations in the described local P2P framework. | Coordinator intervention under the paper's heuristic convergence techniques. | Limits of the coordinator's modeled remit in the studied P2P framework. | SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g06-e12","v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E001","source":"bidding.demand","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"]},"paper_scope_note":"SDR, MMR, and BS are kept separate; the A18 net quantity differs from the A24 independent component; optional step-size control and the divergent loop in the example are not treated as general convergence or necessary dependencies."}});
